' A controller's sticks (`HandleGamePadInput`; `preset classic|extended ai
' none seed 3 start 30`, Paradise Camp), sent as the window's axis events
' (`stick AXIS VALUE`). The left stick held right walks the leader directly
' as the arrow does (from 64,160); the right stick held down pans the
' place's camera as S does; in the tent the left stick's push moves the
' grid's focus, diagonally there (`UseDiagonalGamepadNavigation`); on the
' world map a push down and right selects the place that way. A push is one
' press until the stick comes back to the middle. The axes are read once a
' frame, as v1.2 reads the pad: `stick` lines in a row move them together.
' How far the pan goes depends on the window: the camera stops at the
' place's edge (0,20 at the host's 1280x720, 0,33 at AROS's 640x480).
press escape             ' Back closes the manual v1.2 opens on a new game's first world map (MapScene.cs:687-691)
mapclick 110,122         ' into Paradise Camp
wait 60
stick 0 32767            ' left stick right: walk
wait 29                  ' about 80 px at v1.2's 50 px/s (CONTROLLED_WALK_SPEED): short of the tent, which the click below opens
stick 0 0
wait 2
save                     ' the leader moved right
stick 3 32767            ' right stick down: pan
wait 30
stick 3 0
wait 2
mapclick 177,150         ' the tent
wait 200
stick 0 32767            ' a push right: the floor's first item
wait 2
stick 0 0
wait 2
stick 0 -32767           ' left and down together: a diagonal
stick 1 32767
wait 2
stick 0 0
stick 1 0
wait 2
press escape
wait 10
esc                      ' the world map
wait 10
stick 0 32767            ' down and right together: one press, diagonal
stick 1 32767
wait 2
stick 0 0
stick 1 0
wait 2
quit
